## Python and JavaScript

```python
def lantern_total(samples):
    return sum(value for value in samples if value >= 0)

print(lantern_total([4, 7, 0]))  # 11
```

```javascript
const samples = [4, 7, 0];
const total = samples.reduce((sum, value) => sum + value, 0);
console.log({ total });
```

